Protect SMP-shared mappings after default construction.

The four Device mappings are installed after broad default RAM mappings.
Once published, reject incompatible remaps, additional aliases and removals.
Validate raw mapping arguments before descriptor construction. The mapper
supports lower-48-bit virtual inputs only; its TTBR1 mirror is not an API input.
Rebuilds reset readiness. Inherited MMU-on state cannot start secondary CPUs
without the locally constructed shared mappings. No native validation claim.

